[size=3][color=#f2c078][b]Version 0.9.1 - public beta[/b][/color][/size][/center]

Thanks for trying BG3RTX. This is a [b]public beta[/b]. It has been tested in a limited set of places and on one card only, an [b]RTX 5090[/b]. Your reports decide what gets fixed first.

[img]IMAGE_URL:h_read_first.png[/img]

[list]
[*]The game must use the [b]Vulkan[/b] renderer and [b]DLSS[/b] in its Graphics options. DirectX 11 is not supported, and Ray Reconstruction does not run with FSR, XeSS or TAA.
[*][b]NVIDIA RTX only.[/b] Frame generation 2x needs RTX 40 or newer; 3x and 4x need RTX 50.
[*]Start with [b]Low[/b] and raise settings step by step. There are no tested VRAM recommendations yet, for any card.
[*]The [b]first start[/b] compiles shaders: expect a slower load and some stutter the first time. It is quicker afterwards.
[*]Press [b]Ctrl+Shift+F9[/b] in game to switch all ray tracing off and on. Use it to check whether a problem comes from BG3RTX. You can change the shortcut in the launcher (Advanced).
[*][b]New in 0.9.1:[/b] experimental [b]DLSS 5 Neural Rendering[/b] on its own launcher page (off by default; you provide the runtime), [b]ReShade[/b] compatibility, a cheaper Ultra GI and a fix for DLSS mode changes. See the Changelog.
[*]BG3RTX changes nothing in the game folder, the registry or your saves. Starting the game without the launcher runs the plain game.
[/list]

[img]IMAGE_URL:h_help.png[/img]

[list]
[*][b]Crash at start, or frame generation does nothing:[/b] tick [i]Disable other Vulkan overlays[/i] in the launcher (Help & support), then restart the game.
[*][b]Stalls, missing geometry or crashes after a while:[/b] usually video memory. Lower the preset or resolution and restart the game.
[*][b]An option did not change anything:[/b] some options need a game restart; the launcher says so next to them.
[*]Questions go in this comment thread. Bugs go on the [b]Bugs[/b] tab, one report per problem.
[/list]

[img]IMAGE_URL:h_bugs.png[/img]

A good report gets fixed much faster. Please:
[list=1]
[*][b]Turn on Detailed logging[/b] in the launcher (Help & support), restart the game and reproduce the problem.
[*][b]Save the report.[/b] Right after the problem, open the launcher: [i]Help & support > Report a problem...[/i], preview it, then [i]Save report...[/i] Attach that file. Nothing is uploaded for you; check what it contains before you share it.
[*][b]Add your system:[/b] GPU and VRAM, NVIDIA driver version, game version, and any other graphics mods (ReShade and so on).
[*][b]Add your settings:[/b] the preset, and any options you changed.
[*][b]Say what happened:[/b] act and place, time of day, what you expected and what you saw. A screenshot with Ctrl+Shift+F9 off and on helps a lot.
[/list]
Turn Detailed logging off again afterwards: it writes extra data you do not need for normal play.
[color=#f2c078]Please do not post a save file unless you are asked for one.[/color] If it is needed, you will be told how to include it.

[img]IMAGE_URL:h_known_issues.png[/img]

[list]
[*]Act 2 and most of Act 3 are not systematically tested yet. Reports from there are very welcome.
[*]Sessions of several hours are not tested yet. Long sessions and level changes can hold on to video memory.
[*]Reflections trace the real scene, but a reflected surface that is hidden or off screen keeps the game's own reflection for now.
[*]The first time hair shadows are turned on, shaders compile: a short pause or stutter is expected.
[*]The water flicker at the port is also in the game's own water.
[*]ReShade works, frame generation included. ReShade effects that redo ambient occlusion or global illumination duplicate BG3RTX's work. Other graphics mods and HDR have not been tested.
[*]DLSS 5 Neural Rendering is experimental: it changes the look of the image and costs about 6.7 ms per frame on an RTX 5090 at 3840x1600.
[*]A new game patch can break BG3RTX until it is updated.
[*]Visible hair is the game's own hair. Strand hair is planned for a later update.
[/list]

